<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">People's State of Reuss</h1><p class="st-meta">1919 CE – 1920 CE · capital Gera</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Brief Thuringian republic uniting the two old Reuss principalities before they merged into Thuringia.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Principality of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-reuss-greiz">Reuss Elder Line</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greiz">Greiz</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/principality-of-reuss-younger-line">Principality of Reuss Younger Line</a> at Gera both became free states in November 1918 after their princes abdicated. In April 1919 the two united as the People's State of Reuss, with Gera as capital.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The state was industrial, with textile and machine-building works around Gera and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greiz">Greiz</a>, and its politics were dominated by the Social Democrats and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/independent-social-democratic-party-of-germany">Independent Socialists</a>. It existed mainly to manage the transition from monarchy and to negotiate the union of the small Thuringian states.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>On 1 May 1920 the People's State of Reuss merged with six other states to form the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-state-of-thuringia">Free State of Thuringia</a>. Gera, its capital, became one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia's</a> main industrial cities and later a district capital in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-germany">East Germany</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/peoples-state-of-reuss.jpg" alt="People's State of Reuss" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Mmxx · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Germany_(3-2).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1919 CE – 1920 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Gera</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Volksstaat Reuß</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1920&amp;focus=peoples-state-of-reuss" aria-label="People's State of Reuss on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4955 413 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where People's State of Reuss lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5275 669L5278 675M5275 669L5275 669M5275 669L5300 622M5275 669L5250 665"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5278 675h0M5275 669h0M5300 622h0M5250 665h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5275 669h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5275 669h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Gera. <a href="/atlas?year=1920&amp;focus=peoples-state-of-reuss">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
